<title>FINLAND: Merita arranges $20 mln Latvian credit.</title>
<headline>Merita arranges $20 mln Latvian credit.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Merita Bank said in a statement on Monday it had arranged a $20 million loan to mobile telecommunications operator  Latvian Mobile Telephone Limited.</p>
<p>The lenders were Merita Bank, The Finnish Government Guarantee Fund, Nordiska Investeringsbanken (NIB) and the Investment Bank of Latvia, it said.</p>
<p>A Merita official said the five-year credit was &quot;probably the largest ever single credit&quot; in Latvia. The borrower is 49 percent owned by  Telecom Finland and Swedish  Telia. The majority is owned by Latvian state firms.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
</text>
